1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,839
Every morning the phones start early.

2
00:00:02,839 --> 00:00:04,891
Orders come in by phone and email,

3
00:00:04,891 --> 00:00:07,831
and every one gets keyed in by hand.

4
00:00:07,881 --> 00:00:10,053
Then it's looking up each customer's price,

5
00:00:10,053 --> 00:00:13,341
and chasing PO numbers at the end of the month.

6
00:00:13,592 --> 00:00:15,795
So what if your trade customers could order

7
00:00:15,795 --> 00:00:19,498
for themselves, at their own prices, any time?

8
00:00:19,799 --> 00:00:23,337
Your customer logs in and sees their own agreed trade price.

9
00:00:23,337 --> 00:00:25,221
Never a public one.

10
00:00:25,510 --> 00:00:29,123
One tap on Buy Again repeats last week's order,

11
00:00:29,392 --> 00:00:31,957
they add their PO number, and send it.

12
00:00:31,957 --> 00:00:35,305
From the van, at six in the morning if they need to.

13
00:00:35,521 --> 00:00:37,148
It lands on your order desk.

14
00:00:37,148 --> 00:00:38,981
Your team approves it in one click,

15
00:00:38,981 --> 00:00:41,858
and the PO goes straight onto the invoice.

16
00:00:43,491 --> 00:00:46,324
Customers in Northern Ireland see sterling prices

17
00:00:46,324 --> 00:00:49,415
and twenty per cent VAT, automatically.

18
00:00:49,699 --> 00:00:50,974
Fewer calls.

19
00:00:50,974 --> 00:00:52,655
Fewer keying errors.

20
00:00:52,655 --> 00:00:54,809
Orders around the clock.

21
00:00:54,868 --> 00:00:58,133
Your own trade portal, built and ready to see.

22
00:00:58,133 --> 00:01:00,950
Reply here to book a twenty-minute walkthrough.
